
       1 . BUBBLE SORTING ......
 It takes more time.
 It swap n times using the  bubble one by one.
def bubblesort (arr):
    for i in range(len(arr)):
        for j in range(0,len(arr)-i-1):
            if (arr[j] > arr[j+1]):
               temp = arr[j]
               arr[j] = arr[j+1]
               arr[j+1] = temp
    return arr

arr = list(map (int,input ("enter the value of array \n").split()))
print(bubblesort(arr))

      2.SELECTION SORTING....
It takes same time comparing to bobble sort but it work  in the outer loop
It is more efficient 
It can find the minimum value using that swap that element positions.
      TIME COMPLEXITY : O(nsquare)
      SPACE COMPLEXITY : O(1)
 code::
 
def selectionsort (arr):
    for i in range(len(arr)-1):
        smallest = i
        for j in range(i+1,len(arr)):
            if arr[j] < arr[smallest]:
              smallest = j
        temp = arr[i]
        arr[i] = arr[smallest]
        arr[smallest]= temp
    return arr
arr = list(map (int,input ("enter the value of array \n").split()))
print(selectionsort(arr))
    
